# Lab 3: Host SignalR Chat as ASP.NET Core Web App

Convert the existing WPF desktop SignalR chat client into a fully hosted ASP.NET Core web application with user authentication, Messenger-style UI, async large file transfer, emoji picker, and image preview.

## Existing Codebase

- **Chat.Server**: ASP.NET Core (.NET 8) backend with SignalR [ChatHub](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Hubs/ChatHub.cs#17-21) + Supabase for persistence (users, messages, reactions)
- **Chat.Client**: WPF desktop client (will remain untouched — we add a new web project alongside it)

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> A new project `Chat.Web` will be added to the existing solution. The existing `Chat.Server` and `Chat.Client` projects will **not** be modified. The web app will reuse the same `Chat.Server` backend (SignalR hub + Supabase).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Authentication will use **ASP.NET Core Cookie Authentication** integrated with the existing Supabase `users` table (username/password). This keeps things consistent with the existing [JoinChat](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Hubs/ChatHub.cs#163-270) flow.

> [!WARNING]
> Large file upload (>=1GB) uses chunked upload via a dedicated API endpoint with streaming (`IFormFile` disabled in favor of `Request.Body` streaming). Files are stored on disk in `wwwroot/uploads/`.

## Proposed Changes

### Git Branch

Create branch `lab3-webapp` from `master`.

---

### Chat.Server (Backend Modifications)

#### [MODIFY] [Program.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Program.cs)

- Add CORS policy to allow the web client to connect
- Add cookie authentication middleware
- Add static file serving for uploaded files
- Add a file upload API endpoint (`/api/upload`) that accepts chunked streaming for large files (>=1GB)
- Add an auth API endpoint (`/api/auth/login` and `/api/auth/register`) using Supabase `users` table
- Configure SignalR for large message sizes (file metadata)

#### [MODIFY] [ChatHub.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Hubs/ChatHub.cs)

- Add `[Authorize]` attribute to require authentication
- Add method `SendFileMessage(string user, string fileName, string fileUrl, long fileSize)` for file sharing
- Update [JoinChat](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Hubs/ChatHub.cs#163-270) to work with authenticated context (read username from cookie claims)

#### [NEW] [FileMessage.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Models/FileMessage.cs)

- Model for file message metadata (fileName, fileUrl, fileSize, uploadProgress)

---

### Chat.Web (New Razor Pages Web Client)

#### [NEW] [Chat.Web.csproj](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Web/Chat.Web.csproj)

- ASP.NET Core Web App (.NET 8) with Razor Pages
- SignalR JavaScript client (via `libman` or CDN)

#### [NEW] [Program.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Web/Program.cs)

- Configure Razor Pages + cookie authentication
- Proxy or redirect to Chat.Server for SignalR

> [!NOTE]
> **Revised approach**: Instead of creating a separate `Chat.Web` project, the web frontend will be **hosted directly from `Chat.Server`**. This avoids CORS complexity and keeps SignalR + authentication in one process. Razor Pages will be added to `Chat.Server` directly.

---

### Revised Architecture: Single Project (Chat.Server hosts everything)

#### [MODIFY] [Chat.Server.csproj](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Chat.Server.csproj)

- Add `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Cookies` package
- Add Razor Pages support

#### [MODIFY] [Program.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Program.cs)

- Add cookie authentication services
- Add Razor Pages services
- Add static files middleware
- Add antiforgery middleware
- Map Razor Pages + fallback
- Add file upload endpoint `/api/upload` (streaming, chunked)
- Configure SignalR for large payloads
- Configure Kestrel for large request body (>=1GB)

#### [NEW] [Pages/_ViewImports.cshtml](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Pages/_ViewImports.cshtml)

- Standard Razor Pages imports

#### [NEW] [Pages/Login.cshtml + Login.cshtml.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Pages/Login.cshtml)

- Login page with username/password form
- Validates against Supabase `users` table
- Creates authentication cookie on success
- Register option (creates new user in Supabase)

#### [NEW] [Pages/Register.cshtml + Register.cshtml.cs](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Pages/Register.cshtml)

- Registration page with username/password form
- Creates user in Supabase

#### [NEW] [Pages/Chat.cshtml](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/Pages/Chat.cshtml)

- **Messenger-style chat UI** with the following features:

**Layout:**
- Left sidebar: online users list, user info, disconnect button
- Main area: chat messages with Messenger-style bubbles
  - Incoming messages aligned **left** (grey bubbles)
  - Outgoing messages aligned **right** (blue bubbles)
  - Timestamps, sender names, private message indicators
- Bottom: message input area with recipient selector, emoji button, file attach button

**Emoji Picker:**
- Emoji button opens a floating panel with categorized emoji grid
- Clicking an emoji inserts it into the message input
- Common emojis: 😊😂❤️👍🔥😭🎉💯🙏😎 etc.

**Image Preview:**
- When an image file is shared, it renders as an inline thumbnail in the chat bubble
- Clicking the thumbnail opens the full image in a modal/lightbox
- Drag-and-drop images into the textbox

**Large File Upload:**
- File attach button opens file picker (any file type)
- Files are uploaded via chunked streaming to `/api/upload`
- Progress bar shown during upload
- On completion, a file message is broadcast via SignalR
- Download link appears in chat for recipients

#### [NEW] [wwwroot/css/chat.css](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/wwwroot/css/chat.css)

- Messenger-style CSS: chat bubbles, left/right alignment, emoji panel, file upload progress, responsive layout
- Premium dark/light theme with gradients and micro-animations

#### [NEW] [wwwroot/js/chat.js](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/wwwroot/js/chat.js)

- SignalR JavaScript client connection
- Message rendering (left/right bubble alignment based on sender)
- Emoji picker toggle and insertion
- File upload with chunked `fetch()` and progress tracking
- Image preview rendering in chat bubbles
- Auto-scroll, notifications, recipient selection

#### [NEW] [wwwroot/uploads/](file:///d:/Code/LAB01_ChatClients_WPF/Chat.Server/wwwroot/uploads/)

- Directory for uploaded files (created at runtime)

